	(text "J2  (mates Frontend J2, DF40C-70DS on its bottom face)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.68 139.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "64cef2d3-4c3d-536e-89a6-86a10b036400")
	)
	(text "J4  2 x 35 header, pin n = J2 pin n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 447.9 182.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "386fa67a-b319-53a6-9c84-d18622b3d1c3")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: J1 is the plug half of the Frontend J1 board-to-board pair; the Frontend board (14 layers V17 or V18) presses onto it exactly as it presses onto the FPGA-LDO board. Every J1 contact is wired to the same-numbered pin of the 2.54 mm header J3 (J3 pin n = J1 pin n = Frontend J1 pin n), so any FPGA pin on this connector can be driven or probed with a jumper wire, scope probe or logic-analyser clip. The 61 signal pins are FPGA I/O in banks 14/15/34 at LVCMOS 1.5 V (VCCO_1V5): never apply more than 1.5 V. Pins 14, 15, 27, 30, 34, 41, 50, 66 are ground; pin 32 is VIN_5V (the Frontend 5 V input, fed from block C or from the cable).\n\n2. Source / changes: Structure designed by Claude for this breakout; it is not a manufacturer reference circuit. Net names and pin numbers are copied from the Frontend 14 layers V17 board file (J1 pads) and agree pin for pin with FPGA-LDO A layout V24 J1 (Final Versions row 3). J1 uses the same part, footprint and placement relative to J2 as FPGA-LDO A V24: Hirose DF40C-70DP-0.4V(51), JLC C2692097 (4996 orderable, read 25 Nov 2026 10:58 CST), Hirose DF40 series catalogue via https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C2692097.pdf (mated height 1.5 mm for the (51) suffix, contact rating 0.3 A per pin). J3: YXY-PZ2.54-2X35PIN-DIP, JLC C56434801 (100 orderable, read 25 Nov 2026 10:58 CST; 10 needed for 5 boards), https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C56434801.pdf. Pin directions and I/O standard: Frontend pin file V4 (2026-11-19 10_, Frontend_V57_pins_V4.xdc). Unverified: no series resistors or ESD parts, so a wrong voltage on a header pin reaches the FPGA ball directly; the 0.3 A contact rating limits 5 V fed through J1 pin 32."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.8 335.28 0)
		(size 220 36.8)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ee6b9d48-ba23-5728-b2cf-79c188fe64c8")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: J2 is the plug half of the Frontend J2 board-to-board pair. Every J2 contact is wired to the same-numbered pin of header J4 (J4 pin n = J2 pin n = Frontend J2 pin n). The 60 signal pins are LVCMOS 1.5 V FPGA I/O; pins 14, 15, 27, 34, 41, 50, 66 are ground; pins 68, 69, 70 are VIN_3V3, the OUTPUT of the Frontend 5 V to 3.3 V converter U16 (normally feeding the FPGA-LDO board), shown by LED D3 in block D. Do not feed 3.3 V into these pins.\n\n2. Source / changes: Structure designed by Claude, identical in form to block A. Net names from the Frontend 14 layers V17 board file (J2 pads), equal pin for pin to FPGA-LDO A V24 J2. Parts and stock as block A: DF40C-70DP-0.4V(51) JLC C2692097, https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C2692097.pdf; header JLC C56434801, https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C56434801.pdf (read 25 Nov 2026 10:58 CST). Unverified: as block A; the Frontend has the FPGA pull-downs of pin file V4 on the 88 ASIC inputs, so unconnected input pins read 0."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 309.88 335.28 0)
		(size 220 25.6)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
