	(text "Block C · 5 V input (USB-C or bench) to Frontend VIN_5V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 560 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7610afce-b330-591b-80ee-08633160cee0")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: Optional 5 V supply for running the Frontend on this board without the HDMI cable (the cable normally brings 5 V on J3.19 together with JTAG). A USB-C charger or port (J5, sink only) or a current-limited bench supply on J6 feeds 5V_USB; Schottky D1 passes it to VIN_5V (about 4.6 V) and blocks current back into the USB source or the cable source when both are connected, and blocks a reversed bench supply. R1/R2 (5.1 k) on CC1/CC2 make J5 a USB-C sink so the source turns VBUS on. C1/C2 are local bulk capacitors; D2 lights when VIN_5V is present. VIN_5V reaches the Frontend through J3 pin 32 and J1 pin 32 (one 0.3 A DF40 contact).\n\n2. Source / changes: Structure designed by Claude. CC sink termination Rd = 5.1 k from USB Type-C Cable and Connector Specification Release 2.1, section 4.11.1 / Table 4-24, https://www.usb.org/document-library/usb-type-cr-cable-and-connector-specification-release-21 (D+/D-/SBU unused, no data). J5 HRO TYPE-C-31-M-12 JLC C165948 (422892 orderable), https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C165948.pdf; D1 SS34 3 A 40 V JLC C8678 Basic (2021377), https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C8678.pdf; R1/R2 5.1 k 1% 0603 C23186 Basic (16133213); C1/C2 10 uF 25 V X5R 0805 C15850 Basic (7415432); R3 1 k C21190 Basic (31337561); D2 KT-0805G green C2297 Basic (2663605), https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C2297.pdf; J6 PZ254V-11-02P C492401 (856409). Stock read 25 Nov 2026 10:58 CST. Unverified: the Frontend current from 5 V has not been measured, so whether one DF40 contact (0.3 A) is enough when the board is powered from J5/J6 is open; U16 input with the 0.35-0.5 V diode drop is assumed fine."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
